PTX 2+2W+vector.v2.u64
"Two threads each store both elements of a 16-byte relaxed vector of two 64-bit elements, 1 and 2. A strong vector access of at most 16 bytes is single-copy atomic (D43), so coherence orders the two stores the same way on both elements: the final values come from one store, not one element from each: forbidden."
{
a=0;
b=0;
}
 P0@cta 0,gpu 0                      | P1@cta 1,gpu 0                      ;
 st.relaxed.gpu.v2.u64 a, b, 1, 1    | st.relaxed.gpu.v2.u64 a, b, 2, 2    ;
exists
(a == 1 /\ b == 2)
